=== file: README.md ===
# Pricing claim audit

This on-demand workflow compares supplied pricing-page text with claims from a spreadsheet export. It returns a structured report containing mismatches with supporting page text, ambiguous or partially supported claims for human review, confirmed matches, and reviewer notes.

## Authorization and data handling

Provide `environmentclearance` as `approved` only when the execution environment and use of the configured AI service are authorized for these inputs. If clearance is `unknown`, the workflow asks PricingReviewer before processing. A denied, unconfirmed, or otherwise unrecognized clearance halts the run before the audit agent receives either input.

The audit agent has no tools and cannot send or change anything. Its model must be configured only in an environment where processing these inputs is permitted. If using an external AI service is not permitted, do not run this project with that service.

When claims are ambiguous or only partially supported, the workflow includes them separately and asks PricingReviewer for notes. They are never treated as confirmed matches.

## Run and test

Supply `sourcepagepayload`, `sheetclaimpayload`, and `environmentclearance` for each on-demand run. Route human prompts to PricingReviewer in the approved deployment environment.

Run the logic tests with:

```text
weave test main.loom
```

The tests use scripted model replies and do not require a live model or network access.
